WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.520
There are about a million things you can do
wrong when starting up Pokemon Sun and Moon,

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:11.160
so we've taken it upon ourselves to give you
some tips on what not to do while adventuring

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:16.370
in Alola. Here's are some things to avoid
in Pokemon Sun and Moon.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.779
Don't restart for shiny Pokemon

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:25.350
Sure, it's tempting to restart your game to
try and get a shiny starter Pokemon, but keep

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:31.009
in mind that getting one to spawn is a 1-in-4,000
chance.

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:40.950
“Hahaha...oh my God, I got it. I’m still
shaking.”

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:46.140
And since you have to endure three minutes
of dialogue every time you restart, your time

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:52.660
is probably better spent progressing the game
so you can breed your own shiny Pokemon instead.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:59.320
“OH MY GOD! SHINY ROWLET! SHINY ROWLET!
OH MY GOD! WE GOT IT! WE GOT IT!”

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.870
Don't avoid Trainer battles

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.710
When a nearby Trainer is looking to brawl,
the screen dims, making it easy to avoid the

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:13.119
fights if you want to. But you shouldn't skip
them: not only will your Pokemon get much-needed

00:01:13.119 --> 00:01:18.219
experience, but you'll also build up a good
amount of cash and snag a few items here and

00:01:18.219 --> 00:01:23.090
there. Plus, it's a good idea to clear the
area so if you need to backtrack you won't

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:26.799
have these Trainers attacking you all the
time.

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:28.819
Don't stick with the same team

00:01:28.819 --> 00:01:34.119
It's tempting to keep your original six Pokemon,
especially since they might be your strongest

00:01:34.119 --> 00:01:38.789
and highest level. But mixing and matching
your team isn't just part of the fun — it

00:01:38.789 --> 00:01:43.929
allows you to switch strategies to overcome
specific enemies. And since you can get the

00:01:43.929 --> 00:01:49.999
E. X. P. Share item early on in the game,
it's relatively easy to bring a new, lower-level

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:54.990
Pokemon up to speed with the rest of your
team after a few battles, since it'll get

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.680
half the experience your active Pokemon earns.

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.840
Don't over-level your Pokemon

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:06.310
It may sound weird, but it's possible your
Pokemon could become more powerful than you.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:13.360
Yup, it's true: if you over-level your Pokemon,
they may stop listening to your orders. Instead,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.480
level your team to the proper levels and then
complete the Grand Trials that reward you

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:23.820
with stamps on your Trainer Passport that
allows higher-level Pokemon to follow your

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:24.820
commands.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.430
Don't blow your cash on clothing

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:31.340
One of the coolest features in Pokemon Sun
and Moon is the ability to customize your

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:36.060
character's appearance, from the clothes they
wear to the hairstyles they rock. But while

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:41.200
it's tempting to bling yourself out, make
sure you save enough money for things that

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.480
actually affect gameplay, like Pokeballs,
Revives, Super Potions, and maybe the occasional

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.410
Escape Rope or two. Don't worry, by the end
of the game you'll have enough cash to do

00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:52.620
whatever you want.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.060
Don't neglect your Ride Pokemon

00:02:55.060 --> 00:03:00.380
Your Ride Pager is there for a reason, so
don't walk around like a rube when you can

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:05.700
be charging your way through areas in half
the time with your Tauros. As you continue

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.730
the story, you'll get access to more Ride
Pokemon with different abilities, some of

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:16.239
which can even net you more items, like the
Stoutland and its Search skill that can sniff

00:03:16.239 --> 00:03:21.129
out hidden objects. It's easy to forget that
you have these Ride Pokemon at your service

00:03:21.129 --> 00:03:27.390
until an obstacle is in your way, but be sure
to use them and to use them often, especially

00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:31.840
because they can get you to hidden areas with
cool items to collect.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.299
Don't forget to save

00:03:33.299 --> 00:03:38.230
This seems like a no-brainer, but plenty of
people forget to save their games every so

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:44.659
often. This, of course, can result in losing
precious progress, either in the story or

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:50.500
in training up Pokemon. Thankfully, the game
saves after you trade Pokemon with someone,

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:56.290
so you don't have to worry about losing a
new friend, but there could be worse scenarios.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:04:01.459
Given that the game is on a portable console,
you're always in danger of losing battery

00:04:01.459 --> 00:04:08.180
life in the middle of an important battle
or Trial, so save often. Because you know

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.680
how you'll feel if you don't.

00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:19.030
Don't neglect Pokemon Refresh

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:23.410
Want to build up your Pokemon's affection
and bond with them? Well, that's what Pokemon

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:28.080
Refresh is for. Every so often, you'll see
a "Care" option on the touchscreen of your

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.670
device after a battle. Pressing "Y" will lead
you to the Pokemon Refresh screen and task

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:38.449
you with either cleaning up your Pokemon or
getting rid of their status ailments, like

00:04:38.449 --> 00:04:40.400
paralysis or poison.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:45.520
Not only that, but you can feed them Poke
Beans and pet them to raise their affection

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:50.430
towards you. Once you max out their affection,
they'll be able to do cool things in battle

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:56.530
like dodge attacks in response to your "shouts,"
shake off status effects, and even wish for

00:04:56.530 --> 00:05:02.720
your praise after they land critical hits.
It pays to bond with your Pokemon.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.520
Don't randomly overwrite moves

00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:10.470
Your Pokemon's move list is what gives it
flavor in battle and can be crucial to winning

00:05:10.470 --> 00:05:16.650
matches, especially if you're a competitive
player. With that said, don't just keep deleting

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:21.699
old moves every time your Pokemon levels up
and tries to learn a new skill. The new skills

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:27.240
might seem cool, but it's possible the old
skill is actually better. Luckily, there are

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:32.610
sites to help you study up to see which skills
are best for you and your Pokemon.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.210
Don't ignore the hidden Zygarde cells

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:39.949
If you notice some swirling green or pink
lights anywhere in the world, you should go

00:05:39.949 --> 00:05:46.430
up to them and investigate. These are Zygarde
Cells and Cores, which make up the Pokemon

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:53.080
called, well, Zygarde. It's easy to overlook
them, but it's a good idea to collect as many

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:58.610
of these as you go so that you can create
the 10 percent and 50 percent Forms, eventually

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:05.550
collecting 100/100 elements to create the
100 percent Form. It might take some time,

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:10.800
but if you've ever wanted a Pokemon that kind
of looks like a Transformer, here's your chance.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.490
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:06:15.490 --> 00:06:17.860
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

